    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d613">

                <pb facs="0938" n="818" xml:id="pg818"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500. A 4e/16: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cunningham</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-04-13T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 13,
                                1922—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your 3 April 7, 4 p.m.</p>
                <p>For Arnold.</p>
                <p>Department’s view is that any basis of valuation would be acceptable which in the
                    judgment of the Revision Commission is deemed to correspond most nearly with the
                    actual values which may be anticipated to prevail pending the further revision
                    contemplated by Article 4 of the Customs Convention concluded February 6th.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
